{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_v3cxa53wq2zo3x6dpgp6nfnoocqtxash5kroxbzd3stapxgfg6tq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully implemented the C-to-Rust translation of the chtrie (chained trie hash table) project:\n\n## Summary of Implementation\n\n**`Chtrie::new(n, m)`**: Creates a new trie with at most `n` nodes and alphabet size `m`. Mirrors the C overflow checks:\n- Regulates `n` and `m` to be at least 1\n- Returns `None` if `n` or `m` exceed `i32::MAX`\n- Returns `None` for the same overflow guard from C\n- Allocates `etab` of size `(n-1) + (n-1)/3` and an empty `idxpool` deque\n\n**`walk(from, sym, creat)`**: Looks up an edge in the bucket chain at `(from*alphsz + sym) % ecap`. If found, returns `to`. If not found and `creat != 0`:\n- Reuses an index from the pool (popping the back, mirroring `*--idxptr`), or assigns `idxmax` and increments\n- Returns -1 if the trie is full\n- Prepends a new edge to the bucket's chain\n\n**`del(from, sym)`**: Searches the bucket for a matching edge:\n- If the matching edge is at the head, it's removed and the entire chain following it is dropped (matching the C bug `tr->etab[h] = NULL`), with the head's `to` returned to the pool\n- Otherwise, the matched node is unlinked and its `to` is returned to the pool\n\n**`free()`**: Clears all storage (Rust's `Drop` handles actual deallocation automatically).\n\n**Free functions** `chtrie_walk` and `chtrie_del` delegate to the methods.\n\nThe implementation uses safe Rust throughout (no `unsafe` blocks) and the project compiles cleanly in both dev and release modes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":172,"cache_read_input_tokens":21294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":172,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessi